  "name": "amm-backrun-thin-pools",
  "description": "Ten thin pools over SOL, USDC, JitoSOL, JTO and GEOD for 675 slots. Five large swaps land one at a time: three on Raydium's SOL/JTO pool (one inside its 100 bp fee band, two of 2,000 bp and more), one on the GEOD/USDC pool and one on Orca's SOL/JTO pool. Each is a trigger: the step ends right behind it with its slot open, and the bot, six cycle searchers (two looking at three legs; one, looking at two, tipping 60% in the trigger's slot) and a pool searcher race to close the cycle it opened, in the transaction layer's auction. The deepest cycles run through a third token, JitoSOL or USDC.",
